o cover 2,3,4 with disjoint rows that don't include 0 or 1. Options:\n\n- For element 2: rows 5,9,10. Row 10 also contains 3, so would cover 3 as well. For element 3: rows 7,8,10. Row 8 also contains 4. For element 4: rows 1,4,8.\n\nWe need to cover 2,3,4 exactly once each. Let's consider subcases.\n\nSubcase 1a: Use row 10 (covers 2,3). Then remaining element 4 must be covered by a row that doesn't contain 2 or 3. Row 8 contains 3, so cannot. Row 1 or 4 are fine (they contain 4 only). Also row 8 cannot because it contains 3. So we can choose row 1 or row 4. Also we cannot use row 8. So we have two options: choose row 1 or row 4."}}],"created":1790956666,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":3787,"total_tokens":4555,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-QT8WsaaWn7vwcmdwZj5o77Jw4aEqd4Jk","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":3787,"prompt_ms":450.714,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.11901610773699499,"prompt_per_second":8402.22402676642,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2325.372,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.0317757496740545,"predicted_per_second":329.83969876647694}}